course: dictionary
lesson: 14285
title: Notate: writing down with symbols
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To notate something means to write it down using a special code of signs or symbols. The code might be musical notes, chess moves or dance steps. «Mia will notate her tune on the stave before the concert.» Mia is writing her tune with notes, so notate means to write it in symbols.
explain: The word is about writing in a code, not just any writing. A shopping list in ordinary words is not notating. «Sam notated the chess game, writing each move as e4 and Nf3.» Each move has a short code, and writing the moves that way is notating them.
explain: Look for clues around the word. Music, chess, dance and maths often use signs instead of ordinary words. When a sentence is about signs or steps being written down, notate fits. Check by swapping in "write down using symbols" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Notate means to write something down using a system of signs or symbols.
fact: Music is often notated with notes written on a stave, the set of lines where each note sits.
fact: Chess moves can be notated: «e4» is a short code that names a square on the board.
fact: Dance steps can be notated too, using symbols that show each movement.
fact: Notate is a verb: I notate, he notates, we notated, we are notating.
exercise: «Lily will notate the song on paper so others can play it.» What does notate mean here? | Play it on a drum with no plan | *Write it down using symbols | Sing it loudly | Forget it quickly
exercise: Which of these is an example of notating? | *Writing a chess move as e4 | A shopping list written in ordinary words | Saying a poem out loud | Drawing a picture of a cat
exercise: «The dancers notated their steps in a special code.» Find and copy the word that means written down. | dancers | steps | *notated | special
test: «Ben notated his drum beat with symbols.» What does notated mean? | *Wrote it down using symbols | Hid it under a rug | Played it very fast | Painted it red
test: Which thing can be notated? | A bike ride | A bowl of soup | *A chess game written as moves like e4 | A sunny day
exam: Which sentence uses notate correctly? | Yesterday I notate my cat | I notated my lunch and then I ate it | *The composer notated the tune on paper with notes | The rain notated the window
